      "result_commits": [
        "f4b1c885269e6bc6876100b15059082df6defeb4"
      ],
      "rationale": "Retain generic xHCI callback declaration, phase enum, GPL export and three common reset call sites. SDK enables xHCI PCI/platform, and the pinned emulator binary contains qemu-xhci/nec-usb-xhci model strings; runtime use and a vendor callback consumer remain unverified, so retention is conservative generic source-customization compatibility. Omit the separate DWC3 core/PHY-array callback for the documented physical Synopsys reset-domain/PLL workaround, outside the SDK virtual-controller target; native DWC3 is still compiled. Adapt INIT notification to follow the native Intel 1ms register-access delay, preserving that safety condition before a callback can inspect registers. PRE follows accessible/halted checks; POST follows the first handshake even on error, before CNR readiness. Callbacks can run under host spinlock/IRQ-off, must not sleep or retain hcd, and cannot assume probe allocations exist. Native function code, results and register order are otherwise unchanged. Host shims pass ten port/native cases and detect three premature callback accesses with actual ACK placement; no hardware/boot/runtime compatibility proof.",
      "evidence": [
        "evidence/xhci-reset-review.json",
        "evidence/xhci-reset-hooks-check.json",
        "SECURITY.md: Generic xHCI reset customization"
      ],
      "patch_sha256": "7d8be1549b797412ca16cae6e65dc8567d561cc71a4eb8a2a464cc389227be74",
      "changed_paths": [
        "drivers/android/vendor_hooks.c",
        "drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c",
        "drivers/usb/host/xhci.c",
        "include/trace/hooks/dwc3.h"
      ]
    },
    {
      "commit": "097816659d76e06a767f1125b26b649b331abc91",
      "disposition": "merge-resolution-reconciled-to-lts",
      "result_commits": [
        "d281f3ac0d00d7ae9d409537b1a28f6957701e72",
        "36a0faaa4e3d2dc15cf98ac9467542c64ed85b4c"
      ],
      "rationale": "Every unique remerge hunk in block/blk-zoned.c and drivers/usb/dwc3/core.c examined. Reject ACK reversal of native delayed zone-plug removal/DEAD-state fix; retain that fix and later new-write-after-reset revival handling. Keep native dwc3_readl(dwc, ...) API and native core-reset code; the unique DWC3 core-hook conflict is omitted with its physical PHY workaround, separately scoped in 9326f2e6e8a3. The generic xHCI portion of that parent is retained separately, not misclassified as a DWC3-only callback. Both unique-resolution files remain byte-identical to LTS; failed device-help queries were not used as exclusion evidence.",
